From 440360932da1f83d4e80ac72ee4da72bdb22743f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: loop-uh <loop-uh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:40:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Accept client sockets handed over by the node's 443
 dispatcher

When the node sets XRAY_VPNBOT_HANDOFF_DIR, every TCP-based inbound (raw,
WebSocket, HTTPUpgrade, gRPC, XHTTP) that listens on an IPv4 loopback
address keeps its TCP listener and also takes client sockets on
<dir>/<port>.handoff: a SOCK_SEQPACKET socket whose messages carry TCP
sockets passed with SCM_RIGHTS by the node's 443 dispatcher (vpnbot
node-services go/cmd/sni-dispatch). The dispatcher peeks the ClientHello
without consuming it, picks the inbound by SNI and hands over the client
socket itself, so the inbound reads the untouched ClientHello, sees the
real client address and no proxy stays in the data path.

One function, internet.ListenBeside, wraps the listener each hub opens:
the hub gets a listener that accepts from both, and wraps it exactly as
before (TLS, REALITY, HTTP, gRPC), so both ways in meet the same inbound.
The TCP listener is exactly as configured, so local probes and the
dispatcher's copy path keep reaching the inbound there, and its PROXY
wrapper never sees a handed-over socket: there is no proxy in front of
one, so there is no header. Anything received that is not a TCP socket
is closed; a full backlog holds the sender (backpressure); Close ends
both and frees the path. Without the directory nothing changes.

Capability marker: vpnbot-socket-handoff-v3 (v2 took handed-over sockets
on raw TCP inbounds only; v1 meant a listen path ending in .handoff
instead of TCP; no node used either for traffic).
